+A further authorization regression was conducted on 15 November 2026,
+separately from the recorded experiments. It combined mocked backend
+approval tests with an in-memory EVM running the actual Kernel 0.3.1,
+EntryPoint 0.7, and custom secondary-validator contracts. Positive cases
+covered the Uniswap swap and all four supported Aave actions. Negative
+cases changed protected calldata and batch members or attempted expired,
+reused, incorrectly scoped, or unrestricted authorization. Recording
+contracts observed dispatched calls; they did not model liquidity,
+collateral, or protocol economics. No testnet transaction was submitted.
 
